From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:15:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/48] net: xpon: omci: report failed and unsupported
 attributes with result 9

G.988 (Annex A) defines result 9, "attribute(s) failed or unknown", for
Get and Set. A baseline Get response then carries the values of the
attributes that could be read, the optional-attribute mask (attributes
the ONU does not support) in content bytes 29-30 and the attribute
execution mask (attributes that failed, including those that do not fit)
in bytes 31-32. A Set response carries the same two masks in bytes 2-5.

Except for ME 341, the agent answered every such Get with a lone result
byte: build_response() truncated the content, and the failure paths had
put the mask where the extended layout keeps it anyway. The OLT could not
tell which attribute failed and got none of the values it could have
read. A Set with an attribute the descriptor does not know, or one that
is read-only, came back as "parameter error".

Lay out every Get response through one encoder, shared by the managed
entities with a descriptor, ONU-G, ONU2-G, priority queues, traffic
schedulers and the ANI-G optical levels. A Get that is answered in full
keeps exactly its previous bytes, including the up to 29 bytes of values
the agent has always returned, so nothing the OLT reads today changes.
Answer a Set that names unsupported or read-only attributes with result
9 and the two masks; for a non-datapath ME, apply the attributes that
precede any unknown one, while a datapath ME stays all or nothing.

Count these answers in a new agent_attribute_failures sysfs attribute.

A userspace comparison of every attribute mask on the provisioned ME
instances shows no difference for any Get the agent answered with
success before.

